From: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rockusb: enumerate as a loader device

Rockchip's vendor U-Boot uses bcdUSB 0x0201 for the RockUSB gadget so
RKDevTool identifies the running firmware as Loader rather than Maskrom.
Keep the standard USB 2.0 value for all other download functions.

Signed-off-by: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
@@ -229,6 +229,9 @@
 
 int g_dnl_bind_fixup(struct usb_device_descriptor *dev, const char *name)
 {
+	if (!strcmp(name, "usb_dnl_rockusb"))
+		dev->bcdUSB = cpu_to_le16(0x0201);
+
 	if (!strcmp(name, "usb_dnl_ums"))
 		put_unaligned(ROCKCHIP_G_DNL_UMS_PRODUCT_NUM, &dev->idProduct);
 	else
-- 
